From 071ecdcabbeaaa261da04bc8de647d15bd1c883b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 20:57:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Add SEO foundation: robots, sitemap, canonicals, OG,
 structured data
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The site had no robots.txt, no sitemap, no canonical URLs, no Open Graph
tags, and no structured data. /privacy and /terms set only a title, so
they inherited the homepage's 201-character description verbatim, putting
identical metadata on three URLs.

- Add app/robots.ts and app/sitemap.ts (both previously 404)
- Add per-page canonicals; Next does not infer them
- Shorten the shared description to 154 chars, under the ~160 Google renders
- Give /privacy, /terms and /contact their own descriptions via a
  pageMetadata helper, which also keeps Open Graph page-specific — Next
  merges metadata shallowly, so a page inheriting the root openGraph block
  would advertise the homepage's og:url and og:title as its own
- Retitle /contact from "Contact Us" (24 chars) to carry commercial terms
- Add Organization, WebSite and VideoObject JSON-LD; the homepage VSL is
  already public on YouTube but carried no markup, so it was invisible to
  video search
- Set max-snippet/max-image-preview explicitly, since snippet eligibility
  gates inclusion in AI Overviews

FAQPage, Service and SoftwareApplication schema are deliberately omitted:
Google deprecated FAQ rich results in May 2026, Service earns no rich
result, and SoftwareApplication requires an aggregateRating that would be
self-serving without third-party review data.

Verified: build passes, and /robots.txt, /sitemap.xml, JSON-LD and
per-page canonical/OG tags all render correctly against next start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JzqKZ2Fpevm9Vp1hMULwPf
