From 3fe6e8c80651de21498723e908abfda72bf9c20d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 21:00:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Add weekly SEO report workflow posting to Slack

Runs Mondays, crawls the live site, diffs against the previous run, and
posts a grouped summary to a Slack incoming webhook.

- scripts/seo/audit.py: stdlib-only crawler checking robots/sitemap/HTTPS
  and the apex redirect type site-wide, plus title, description, canonical,
  H1, word count, OG, JSON-LD, image alt text and response time per page
- scripts/seo/report.py: builds Slack Block Kit output, grouping an issue
  affecting N pages into one line rather than N, and reports what was fixed
  or introduced since the previous run
- .github/workflows/seo-report.yml: weekly schedule plus manual dispatch

The webhook is read from the SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL secret and is never
committed. State is persisted to .github/seo-state.json in the repo rather
than actions/cache, since a weekly job sits on the 7-day cache eviction
boundary and would frequently find the cache gone.

Verified with a dry run against the live site.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JzqKZ2Fpevm9Vp1hMULwPf
