From 81e9243274eee921d4d51bc23b2b0cc3eb855aaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 21:03:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Run the SEO check daily but notify only on change

A daily crawl of a four-page site produces identical findings every day,
and a recurring notification that never varies stops being read. Running
daily still catches indexing and regression events within a day rather
than up to a week.

- --only-on-change: post only when the issue set differs from the previous
  run; state is written either way so a change is not re-reported forever
- --weekly-digest: Monday posts regardless, so a quiet week stays
  distinguishable from a job that silently stopped working
- Schedule moved from weekly to daily

Verified all three paths: first run posts, unchanged run stays silent,
digest run posts anyway.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JzqKZ2Fpevm9Vp1hMULwPf
